      "content": "The band check uses the exact scaled price, but priceText rounds the returned candidate to six decimal places. For stock entry '0.000115' and lastMark '0.000011', the exact candidate 0.0000115 is within 5%, but the returned '0.000012' is about 9.1% above the last Mark. Thus accepting the suggestion can produce a price that fails the same check. Validate the representable candidate after formatting (and skip the suggestion if it is zero or outside the band), and add a precision-boundary regression test.",
